  "summary": "Messages queue is cleared. All 7 refill messages were decided under RBC-RX-05 and closed; 1 of them arrived while I was working. Three results also came in partway through and changed two of my decisions, so I reversed or corrected those orders before anything was dispensed.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg — not refilled, needs your review.**\n- At first I renewed it for 90 days. The August St. Brigid potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed sample, so it didn't count; the last valid potassium was 4.5 from January. I also ordered a BMP to repeat it (sr-t0002).\n- Then a new St. Brigid BMP arrived, drawn 10/20 on a good sample: potassium 5.8. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001).\n- Review task task-t0014 is with you. The old order mr-00283 stayed stopped, so he has no active lisinopril order. His hernia repair is now 11/12.\n- I sent him a corrected message. sr-t0002 is still on order.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030), lisinopril 20 mg — not refilled, needs your review.**\n- At first I renewed it. The lab then corrected his 10/6 creatinine to 1.49 (it had been reported as 1.36). That is 35.5% above the 1.10 before the 9/18 dose increase, which the protocol treats like a potassium of 5.5 or higher.\n- I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0003). Review task task-t0015 is with you; mr-00295 stayed stopped, so he has no active lisinopril order. His 30-day supply has run out.\n\n**Samuel Price, metformin 1000 mg twice daily — renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004).\n- His corrected kidney function (eGFR) is 58, and the 8/19 outside HbA1c of 7.1% counts as recent.\n- One order covers his own message and both pharmacy requests.\n- He got a corrected message covering both drugs.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031), metformin 500 mg twice daily — renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007).\n- The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error (wrong patient's specimen), so I used 92 from 9/28. His HbA1c of 6.9% is also from 9/28.\n\n**Marcus Webb, lisinopril 10 mg — renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0013).\n- At first he had no BMP in the past 12 months, so I gave a 30-day supply and ordered a BMP (sr-t0006).\n- A valid BMP from 10/22 then arrived (potassium 4.6, creatinine 1.04), so I replaced that with the 90-day order and sent him an update.\n- The BMP order sr-t0006 is now redundant and needs cancelling — I don't have a tool for that, so task-t0019 asks you to cancel it.\n\nEach patient has a telephone note: doc-t0020, doc-t0021 and doc-t0022.\n\nYour results queue is still open. I acted on the 3 new results for these patients (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) but left them for you, since you asked only about messages. The 8 older results for other patients are untouched, and two of them are critical potassium values: 6.3 for pt-0016 and 6.4 for pt-0008.",
